# LeakSanitizer suppressions for FalkorDB-rs flow tests.
#
# Suppress leaks from C dependencies and Redis itself that are reachable
# at exit by design (long-lived globals; daemons rely on the OS to
# reclaim). These are not bugs in falkordb-rs.

# GraphBLAS global workspace and matrices. `LAGraph_Finalize` releases
# user-visible matrices but GraphBLAS keeps internal global slabs alive
# until process exit.
leak:GB_Global_malloc_function

# Dynamic loader thread-local error buffer.
leak:_dlerror_run

# Redis client/server allocations that live until process exit.
leak:createRawStringObject
leak:createEmbeddedStringObject
leak:readQueryFromClient
leak:_sdsnewlen

# libc-internal thread-local destructor registrations. The main thread's
# entries fire via the libc atexit machinery, which runs after ASAN's
# leak check has already printed its report.
leak:__cxa_thread_atexit_impl

# Dynamic linker (ld-linux.so) startup allocations — not freed at exit.
leak:ld-linux-x86-64.so
